WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  here's the line separating the us from  mexico  it's been a slow train coming for those  who want to cross it legally  and the pandemic has made things worse  with u.s immigration courts closed for  months  there are thousands of migrants stuck in  mexico who need them open to process  their asylum requests  the us has put them in a plan called mpp  which means they have to wait in mexico  while their asylum process plays out  even though they're from other countries  geraldo fled brazil he says because of  the threat of violence  he arrived in border city juarez 10  months ago  but is still waiting for his first court  date  it was for march 14 of this year but  that was changed because of the pandemic  to december 15th  now is for the 10th of may of next year  geraldo his son and his wife are  spending christmas in a shelter  many of the tens of thousands of people  that have been ordered to wait in mexico  in the mpp  program will be doing the same  some migration lawyers are worried that  they could miss the one year deadline to  start the asylum process altogether  louis torres hopes that's not the case  but she is concerned about the  well-being  of those she's trying to help  it's a complicated situation for their  health and basic needs  it's really uncertain what's going to  happen to them and that  generates anxiety just being here  waiting not knowing how to follow up  with the process  church is one of many along the border  which have been turned into shelters  he's seen hope among those now under his  care that a new u.s administration could  help them  i don't know who was happier about  biden's victory the americans or those  stuck here in the asylum process  because it means for them an end to  their stay in mexico so that they can  follow their dreams  president-elect joe biden had promised  to end the mpp  program on his first day in office now  his incoming administration  has signaled it will take more time and  there are questions  about what will then happen to those  spending this christmas in shelters  john holman al jazeera

